
  M80 -- MULTI-ROUND ALTERNATION vs THE SINGLE-PASS RESIDUAL

  Eq. (1) maxes over two single-pass block orders. A segregated utility can instead
  re-study each track against the other's prior approvals, repeatedly, with no tariff
  reform at all. If that fixed point recovers the residual, the paper's central noun
  is wrong. Alternation >= single-pass sequential by construction.

